dek: Twelve accounting firms with a verified City of Los Angeles address. What each one charges. The eight
  we cut, and why.
quickAnswer: HCVT is the best accounting firm in Los Angeles for high net worth families and family offices.
  GHJ is the strongest choice for nonprofits and for entertainment royalty audits. Armanino is the only
  firm here that publishes a price, at $18,487 a year for its startup bundle. Eight firms that rank for
  this search did not qualify, most of them on address.
keyTakeaways:
- HCVT is the largest Los Angeles based firm on this list. It reports more than 800 team members and over
  100 partners and principals.
- Armanino publishes the only price. Its startup bundle costs $18,487 or $26,887 a year.
- Miller Kaplan prints the heading "Los Angeles" above a Burbank address on its own locations page.
- Five of the twelve firms carry an SEC or PCAOB finding. Each one is named inside that firm's entry.
- Kruze Consulting and Propeller Industries rank for Los Angeles searches with no Los Angeles office.
lastUpdated: '2026-08-30'
datePublished: '2026-08-30'
metaTitle: 'Best Accounting Firms in Los Angeles: 12 Verified in 2026'
metaDescription: Twelve accounting firms in Los Angeles ranked by address, ownership and regulator record.
  Our picks for small business, startups and high net worth.
intro: Every list of the best accounting firms in Los Angeles mixes three different things. It mixes firms
  inside the city with firms in Burbank and Beverly Hills. It mixes independent partnerships with firms
  owned by buyout funds. It mixes clean records with records the firm itself does not publish. This ranking
  checked all three, one address and one regulator filing at a time.
comparisonHeading: Best accounting firms in Los Angeles at a glance
