items:
- rank: 1
  name: HCVT
  url: https://www.hcvt.com
  startingPrice: Not published. HCVT publishes no fee, rate or range on its services or contact pages.
  bestFor: High net worth families, family offices and closely held companies that want the largest Los
    Angeles based firm.
  description: |-
    HCVT calls itself "the largest, Los Angeles-based public accounting firm and the 31st largest firm nationally." It made that claim in its own partner announcement of 5 January 2026. The same release reports more than 800 team members and over 100 partners and principals.

    The client description is unusually specific. HCVT names "public and closely held companies; high-net-worth individuals and families and their related entities; and family offices." Business Management and Family Office is a named service line rather than a page inside tax.

    Ownership is stated plainly. HCVT describes itself as an independent member of Moore North America. Its news page carries no 2025 or 2026 announcement of a sale, a merger or an outside investment.

    One fact belongs in any ranking of this firm. The Securities and Exchange Commission censured HCVT on 13 September 2018 and fined it $300,000. The order covered independence violations across 57 private fund audits and six broker dealer audits. It also barred the firm for one year from Custody Rule, broker dealer and public company audit work.
  pros:
  - Its West Los Angeles and Encino offices cover the Westside and the Valley from the same firm.
  - Publishes both a headcount and a partner count, which four firms here do not.
  - Names Media and Entertainment as an industry alongside private wealth, so one firm covers both sides
    of a talent client.
  - Posted a tax alert on 11 August 2026, so the technical content is current.
  cons:
  - The 2018 SEC order appears nowhere on hcvt.com, so a buyer has to find it at the SEC.
  - Its January 2026 release says fourteen offices while its locations page lists sixteen.
  - The West Los Angeles office has no working page of its own, and three likely URLs return 404.
  - Its only Instagram account is a recruiting account rather than a firm account.
  founded: '1991'
  headquarters: 11444 W Olympic Blvd, 11th Floor, Los Angeles, CA 90064. A second Los Angeles office sits
    at 15760 Ventura Blvd, Suite 1700, Encino.
  founders: Phil Holthouse, Jim Carlin and John Van Trigt
