- rank: 2
  name: GHJ
  url: https://www.ghjadvisors.com
  startingPrice: Not published. GHJ publishes no fee or range on any page.
  bestFor: Nonprofits, and entertainment companies that need royalty and profit participation audits.
  description: |-
    GHJ runs a practice almost nobody else publishes. Profit Participation Services audits royalties, licensing and participation statements for entertainment clients. That work sits beside a nonprofit practice covering arts organisations, clinics and private foundations.

    The firm was Green Hasson Janks until it rebranded. GHJ reports nearly 300 professionals and 26 partners as of 2 February 2026. The firm describes itself as an independent member of HLB.

    It grew again in late 2025. Blueprint CFO, a Southern California fractional finance firm, joined GHJ effective 1 November 2025.

    The site has not kept up with the firm. Its footer still reads Green Hasson & Janks LLP. A January 2021 release is still live claiming 160 staff and 15 partners, which is roughly half the current figures.
  pros:
  - Its headquarters is the only Downtown Los Angeles office on this list that is also the firm's main
    office.
  - Royalty and participation auditing is a genuine specialism, and no other firm here publishes one.
  - Publishes International Desks for China, Germany and India. Few firms this size do.
  - Its fractional CFO capability arrived by merger rather than by hiring, so it started with an existing
    client base.
  cons:
  - The news index is broken. Three separate URLs either return 404 or time out.
  - The About page states no founding year. The 1953 date appears only inside press release boilerplate.
  - Its Buffalo office is labelled "New York". Most readers will read that as New York City.
  - Three versions of the firm name are in circulation across one website.
  founded: '1953'
  headquarters: 700 S. Flower St., Suite 3300, Los Angeles, CA 90017
