- rank: 3
  name: Armanino
  url: https://www.armanino.com
  startingPrice: $18,487 a year for the Launch tier and $26,887 a year for the Scale tier. Both require
    a one year contract. The Tailored tier is quoted on request.
  bestFor: Funded startups that want to know the annual cost before the first call.
  description: |-
    Armanino is the only firm in this ranking that publishes a price. Its Startup Tax and Bookkeeping Bundle names three tiers: Launch, Scale and Tailored.

    The two priced tiers buy the same three things. Each covers bookkeeping, tax compliance and R&D credit work. The tax line names a federal Form 1120, one state income tax return, ten forms 1099 and a Delaware franchise tax report. The credit line covers the calculation, the payroll tax offset and a Section 174 analysis. What separates them is a ceiling rather than a feature. Launch stops at 50 transactions and $250,000 of net taxable income. Scale stops at 100 transactions and $10 million in assets.

    Ownership needs stating and cannot be sourced to the firm. Further Global Capital Management lists Armanino as a portfolio company and gives the year as 2024. Armanino's own press release index stops in January 2023 and says nothing about it.

    The audit record is public. The Public Company Accounting Oversight Board issued inspection report 104-2025-001 on 21 November 2024. Four of the four audits reviewed carried Part I.A deficiencies.
  pros:
  - Three City of Los Angeles offices, more than any other firm here.
  - A published annual figure lets a founder budget without a sales call, which nothing else on this list
    allows.
  - Names a Southern California regional leader, so the LA relationship has an owner.
  - Reports 2,500 or more employees, which is the deepest bench in this ranking.
  cons:
  - A deficiency rate of four out of four is the worst inspection result of any firm ranked here.
  - The bundle assumes a Delaware C corporation, since the named filings include a Delaware franchise
    tax report. Any other structure lands in the unpriced tier.
  - The site publishes no founding year and no footer year at all.
  - Attest work, meaning audits and reviews that outsiders rely on, sits in a different legal entity from
    advisory. Only one of the two is a licensed CPA firm.
  headquarters: '777 S Figueroa St #2600, Los Angeles, CA 90017. Two more Los Angeles offices sit at 2121
    Avenue of the Stars, 15th Floor, and 21650 W Oxnard St, Suite 2400, Woodland Hills.'
  comparisonValues:
