  name: SingerLewak
  url: https://www.singerlewak.com
  startingPrice: Not published. SingerLewak publishes no fee or range on any page.
  bestFor: Mid market and venture backed companies working toward an audit committee or an IPO.
  description: |-
    SingerLewak reports 450 or more employees and 80 or more partners and directors. It has operated since 1959 and works from nine states.

    Its published client types run wider than most. The homepage names credit unions, governments, nonprofits, closely held businesses, venture and private equity backed companies, and high net worth individuals.

    Recent content shows where the firm actually sits. It publishes on audit committee governance, IPO readiness, Sarbanes Oxley compliance and forensic accounting. That is a public company and pre-IPO orientation rather than a small business one.

    The firm has combined with at least seven other practices, including Farber Hass Hurley Ventura County in February 2025. It publishes no statement of its own ownership structure anywhere on the site.
  pros:
  - Published a podcast episode on 20 August 2026, the most recent dated content of any firm here.
  - Two City of Los Angeles offices covering the Westside and the Valley.
  - Names both a partner count and a headcount, which most firms here do not.
  - No SEC or PCAOB action was found against the firm.
  cons:
  - Acquired practices keep their old names as divisions. The SingerLewak headcount therefore understates
    the real footprint.
  - Every address is printed as a street and a zip with the city only in the heading, so a copied address
    is incomplete.
  - The contact hub page carries no addresses and no social links.
  - No ownership or alliance statement exists on the site, which is unusual for a firm rolling up practices
    across nine states.
