  name: MGO
  url: https://www.mgocpa.com
  startingPrice: Not published. MGO publishes no fee or range on any page.
  bestFor: Government agencies, cannabis operators and other clients in heavily regulated sectors.
  description: |-
    MGO runs two practices that almost no Los Angeles firm publishes together. One is state and local government work. The other is cannabis, including guidance for medical operators on federal rescheduling.

    The firm reports more than 500 professionals and 80 or more partners across 15 offices. Two of those offices are in India. Its Los Angeles office is in Century City.

    Its five service lines are assurance, tax, consulting, outsourcing and private client services. It names public companies, private businesses, government agencies and high net worth individuals as clients.

    The site is the weak part. MGO says "Founded in 1987" and "more than 35 years of experience" on the same page, which is wrong by four years in 2026. Its newest news item is dated 30 April 2026.
  pros:
  - Public sector audit work is a real barrier to entry, and MGO publishes more of it than anyone else
    here.
  - Its India offices give it an offshore delivery option that most firms this size do not have.
  - Publishes a full executive team with named chief officers for quality, risk and innovation.
  - Holds PCAOB inspection reports for both 2022 and 2024 with no enforcement action attached.
  cons:
  - Four months without a published news item is the slowest content cadence of any firm ranked here.
  - The contact page carries no addresses, so a visitor with 13 offices to choose from has to find a second
