- rank: 11
  name: Rose Snyder & Jacobs
  url: https://www.rsjcpa.com
  startingPrice: Not published. Rose Snyder & Jacobs publishes no fee or range on any page.
  bestFor: Entrepreneurs and family owned businesses that want one office and a named partner.
  description: |-
    Rose Snyder & Jacobs has run from one Encino office since 1976. Its homepage marks a 50th anniversary in 2026.

    The firm sorts its clients into four groups on the homepage. Those are public companies, entrepreneurs and family owned businesses, and high net worth families. A fourth group covers real estate, biotech, technology and nonprofits.

    Family Wealth Services is a named service line. Trust and estate planning and intergenerational wealth transfer sit inside it. The business side is described as strategic tax planning, cash flow insight and business succession planning.

    The audit record needs stating. The PCAOB issued inspection report 104-2024-172 on 24 October 2024 covering the firm's 2023 audits. Both of the two audits reviewed carried Part I.A deficiencies.
  pros:
  - One office and nine named partners means a client is unlikely to be handed between locations.
  - All three founding partners are still listed, which is rare at 50 years.
  - Mergers and acquisitions and international tax are separate named services, which is wide coverage
    for a firm this size.
  - The firm links a Yelp profile from its own site, so its public reviews are easy to find.
  cons:
  - A deficiency in two of two audits reviewed is a poor inspection result, even on a small sample.
  - Its blog runs syndicated tax content rather than firm writing, so the publishing rate overstates the
    firm's own output.
  - No managing partner or chief executive title is published, so there is no named point of accountability.
  - No total headcount is published, only the partner and director names.
