  name: Grobstein Teeple
  url: https://www.gtllp.com
  startingPrice: Not published. Grobstein Teeple publishes no fee or range on any page.
  bestFor: Receiverships, insolvency work and disputes that need a court ready accountant.
  description: |-
    Grobstein Teeple is built around distress rather than compliance. Its named practices include Restructuring and Insolvency, Litigation Support and Forensic Accounting, Independent Fiduciary, E-discovery and Cybersecurity.

    Howard Grobstein works as a receiver and trustee. The firm publishes explainers on how a receivership works, which is not content a general tax practice produces.

    It is the youngest firm on this list, founded in 2013. Six partners and four principals are named. It joined the Alliott Global Alliance on 1 July 2025.

    The office list needs reading carefully. Seven locations are published and four of them are marked "(mail only)." The real footprint is three California offices, one of which is the Woodland Hills base.
  pros:
  - Independent fiduciary and e-discovery are published services, which almost no accounting firm offers.
  - A cybersecurity practice inside a CPA firm is unusual and useful in a forensic engagement.
  - Both founders are named with titles, and both are still running the firm.
  - No SEC or PCAOB action was found against the firm.
  cons:
  - The site publishes no client type at all, so a buyer cannot tell whether the firm wants their work.
  - Its startup and entrepreneur positioning belongs to an affiliate firm rather than to Grobstein Teeple.
  - Its Phoenix office lists a Tempe street address with a Las Vegas zip code.
  - Its own alliance announcement misspells the firm name as Gropstein Teeple.
